OL,3,GNEWSAThousands still without power
OL,4,Aafter Storm Boelo batters Scotland
OL,5,
OL,6,FTens of thousands of homes across
OL,7,FScotland remain without power while the
OL,8,FMet Office has issued a new weather
OL,9,Fwarning in the aftermath of Storm
OL,10,FBoelo.
OL,12,FA 60-year-old man died as the second
OL,13,Fnamed storm in a matter of days brought
OL,14,Fheavy flooding and wind gusts in some
OL,15,Fareas of up to 85mph (137km/h).
OL,17,FRichard Baines, the long-serving
OL,18,Fcurator of Logan Botanic Garden near
OL,19,FStranraer, is understood to have been
OL,20,Fwalking near his home in Mid Kelton,
OL,21,Fjust outside Castle Douglas, when he
OL,22,Fwas hit by a falling tree.
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,424,420,260,160,0,100
